    "q-59700": {
      "dom_id": "step-q59700",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "Kevin, a farmer, prepares fodder annually for his cows. He wants to determine how the weight of fodder changes as the number of cows changes. What is an appropriate unit for Kevin's purpose?",
      "worked_solution": "We *measure the change* in the weight of fodder, as *we change* the number of cows. Consequently, any appropriate unit must take the form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{unit of weight}}{\\text{number of cows}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, among the given options, the only correct one is $\\frac{\\text{kg}}{\\text{cow}}.$",
